id: pm-github-q4uz
title: Refuse reusable sync runs outside the caller default branch
description: "Track https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/128. Add a first-step fail-closed ref guard with injection-safe environment inputs, document caller behavior, and execute real workflow shell contract tests without changing the remaining pipeline."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-github#128"
created_at: "2026-10-15T20:46:41.947Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T06:24:41.008Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-16T06:24:40.999Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-16T00:42:36.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: First-step guard refuses non-default refs and accepts schedule and workflow_dispatch on the default branch; behavioural revert fails; npm and Bun release gates pass at unchanged thresholds.
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T20:46:55.457Z",codex-agent,Starting #128 from main including #130. Add a first-step Bash string comparison using env-bound caller ref/default branch; preserve all later workflow content. Execute the first step for default and non-default refs and prove refusal disappears when only the guard is removed. Document that callers need no guard; run both unchanged release gates under isolated Git identity.
  "2026-10-15T20:48:13.818Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: removed only Require caller default branch from the real workflow and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"first workflow step refuses\" test/import-gate.test.ts. Result: 0 passed, 1 failed; refs/heads/feature/sync returned exit 0 instead of required 1. Restored the guard; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"caller default branch|first workflow step\" test/import-gate.test.ts passed 3/3, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. After removing the guard, the entire workflow is byte-for-byte identical to baseline 3f64d8b (main including #130). The guard uses env inputs and string comparison without a Bash regex."
  "2026-10-15T21:25:15.228Z",codex-agent,"npm run release:check passed under isolated HOME and Git configuration: 679/679 tests, 0 failures/skips/cancellations/todos; 13 authored modules at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage (10040/10040 lines, 10040/10040 statements, 255/255 functions, 2832/2832 branches). Typecheck, build, 158 documented declarations, lint, zero-duplication threshold, privacy, production audit (0 vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, changelog check, and release attestation all passed at unchanged thresholds. Starting bun run release:check next."
  "2026-10-15T22:01:13.539Z",codex-agent,"bun run release:check passed under isolated HOME and Git configuration: 679/679 tests, 0 failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Exact coverage matches npm: 13 authored modules, 10040/10040 lines and statements, 255/255 functions, 2832/2832 branches (100/100/100/100). All static, privacy, audit, packing, changelog and attestation gates passed at unchanged thresholds. Linked focused tests also passed through pm test --run --progress (3/3). Ready for review; callers must repin the reusable workflow to receive this guard. No PM CLI/SDK defect or UX gap encountered. Item remains in_progress and will not be closed."
  "2026-10-15T22:13:02.181Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: all three unresolved review threads are valid against the workflow. The schedule contract must not depend on a repository object in the payload; workflow_dispatch includes repository metadata. GitHub documents that reusable github context belongs to the caller and GET repos/{owner}/{repo} returns default_branch. Resolve via authenticated gh first, fall back only to a present payload default, validate and fail closed before checkout, then carry the result through checkout, reset, PR lookup/create, links and body. Add real Bash payload tests with an injected gh executable and a real trunk Git fixture. Other workflow bytes and release thresholds stay unchanged. Sources: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/events-that-trigger-workflows#schedule ; https://docs.github.com/en/webhooks/webhook-events-and-payloads#workflow_dispatch ; https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/reusing-workflow-configurations#github-context ; https://docs.github.com/en/rest/repos/repos#get-a-repository"
  "2026-10-15T22:17:40.447Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 implementation and behavioural revert proofs: restored focused command node --test --test-name-pattern=\"caller default branch|first workflow step|workflow credentials\" test/import-gate.test.ts passes 7/7 (zero fail/skip/cancel/todo). Reverting only API resolution to payload-only branch initialization makes the realistic schedule-without-repository test fail 0/1: Bash exits 1 instead of 0 and compares refs/heads/main against refs/heads/. Restoring resolution passes. Separately reverting only sync preparation to origin/main makes the no-main contract and real trunk Git fixture fail 0/2: the fixture reaches preparation and exits 128 with invalid reference origin/main. Restoring propagation passes. The trunk fixture has no main branch and verifies guard output, checkout binding, origin/trunk reset, both PR lookup/create bases, tracker links and PR text. README and caller example now describe API/fallback/fail-closed behavior. Typecheck, lint and diff whitespace checks pass. Full npm and Bun gates follow at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-15T22:20:49.629Z",codex-agent,"Linked tests passed through pm test pm-github-q4uz --run --progress: 7/7, no failures/skips/cancellations/todos, under isolated HOME and Git config. The first npm release gate stopped at test compilation because the new spread environment needed an explicit NodeJS.ProcessEnv annotation. Added the annotation; npm run build:test now passes. No runtime behavior changed. Verified 17 of 21 workflow step blocks byte-identical outside the four affected steps and the adjacent default-branch comment; no main literal remains in the reusable workflow. Restarting both complete gates at unchanged thresholds. PM CLI usage note: files/docs additions each take one value; separate calls confirmed existing links without mutation."
  "2026-10-15T23:04:29.386Z",codex-agent,"The complete npm test stage reached 680/681 passing; the sole failure was the unchanged attestation scanner conservatively treating the dynamic gh executable variable as an unknown publish path. Changed only that command seam to literal gh api and inject the test executable through PATH instead. This keeps the attestation policy unchanged and retains real Bash API-boundary tests without SDK mocks. Attestation regressions now pass 8/8. Re-ran both behavioural reverts on the PATH seam: payload-only resolution fails 0/1 with refs/heads/; origin/main propagation fails 0/2 including the real trunk fixture. Restored the fixes. A separate direct focused invocation inherited global pm and caused fixture setup drift; corrected the invocation to the repo-pinned CLI PATH. The release scripts already provide the pinned PATH. Restarting complete npm and Bun gates after the restored focused recheck."
  "2026-10-15T23:06:53.872Z",codex-agent,"Restored PATH-seam focused tests pass 7/7, and attestation tests pass 8/8. Full npm and Bun gates will run against identical tracked content in separate package copies, each with isolated HOME/Git configuration and independent coverage files. The Bun validation copy must reproduce the staged Git tree exactly before its gate runs; no policy, threshold, source inventory, lockfile or package pin changes."
  "2026-10-16T00:12:16.006Z",codex-agent,"Final npm run release:check passed under isolated HOME/Git configuration: 681/681 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Thirteen authored modules have exact 100/100/100/100 coverage: 10040/10040 lines and statements, 255/255 functions, 2832/2832 branches, zero skipped source. Static checks, privacy, zero-duplication threshold, production audit (0 vulnerabilities), pack, changelog and attestation all passed unchanged. Final linked PM tests also passed 7/7 via node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-github-q4uz --run --progress --timeout 600. The identical-tree Bun copy has passed 681/681 tests; its coverage merge is now running after npm aggregation, limiting concurrent merge memory."
  "2026-10-16T00:16:44.905Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 complete: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed 681/681 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, under isolated HOME/Git configuration. The Bun validation copy exactly matched staged Git tree 1e8657e1bd73999c0b25f6dac70534280ca4f243; source and docs still match that tree, with only later tracker evidence additions. Both receipts match: 13 authored modules, 10040/10040 lines and statements, 255/255 functions, 2832/2832 branches, exact 100/100/100/100 with no skipped source. Static, privacy, zero-duplication, production audit, pack, changelog and attestation gates all passed unchanged. Final linked PM tests passed 7/7; focused attestation tests passed 8/8. All three review threads are valid, with the two non-main threads sharing one fix and proof. Current PATH-seam reverts fail 0/1 for payload-only schedule resolution and 0/2 for origin/main preparation; restored tests pass. No main literal remains in the reusable workflow. Caller repinning remains necessary; live caller schedules were not changed or executed. No PM CLI/SDK defect identified; files/docs additions take one value per call. Releasing the claim and leaving the item in_progress for orchestrator verification; no review-thread replies/resolutions or mentions were sent."
